      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the magnitude of a complex number \\( z = a + bi \\), we use the formula \\( |z| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2} \\).\n\nIn this case, \\( a = \\frac{1}{2} \\) and \\( b = -\\frac{3}{8} \\).\n\nTaking the magnitude, we first square the real and imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\left|\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i\\right| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(-\\frac{3}{8}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{9}{64}}\n$$\n\nAdding the fractions:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{9}{64}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{64} + \\frac{9}{64}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}} = \\frac{5}{8}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the given complex number is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\frac{5}{8}}\n$$",
