      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The solution process is as follows:\n\nFirst, we convert the complex number to polar form. The magnitude of a complex number can be found by taking the absolute value. What is this?\n\n\\begin{align\\*}\n\\left|\\frac12 - \\frac38i\\right|&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2+\\left(-\\frac38\\right)^2}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac14+\\frac{9}{64}}\\\\\n&=?\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac2{16}+\\frac{9}{64}}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac4{32}+\\frac9{64}}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac4{32}+\\frac3{32}}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac7{32}}\\ [= r]\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{r^2}{a}}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{7/32}{1}}\\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}\n\\end{align\\*}\n\n\\boxed{\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{16}}\n\nGreat job! I solved this problem using my very own approach. Let me know about any questions",
